1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:03,569
AI agents have become part of how we code.

2
00:00:03,569 --> 00:00:05,287
We use Codex, Claude Code,

3
00:00:05,287 --> 00:00:07,052
and Kimi to build features,

4
00:00:07,052 --> 00:00:09,525
review changes, and explore ideas.

5
00:00:09,525 --> 00:00:10,604
And more and more,

6
00:00:10,604 --> 00:00:13,437
that work runs on remote development servers.

7
00:00:13,437 --> 00:00:15,693
Usually, more than one.

8
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:19,947
But working over SSH comes with a few rough edges.

9
00:00:19,947 --> 00:00:21,248
When your connection drops,

10
00:00:21,248 --> 00:00:23,964
the agent in that terminal can stop with it.

11
00:00:23,964 --> 00:00:25,915
Pasting a screenshot into a remote

12
00:00:25,915 --> 00:00:28,017
terminal doesn't really work.

13
00:00:28,017 --> 00:00:29,305
And once sessions are spread

14
00:00:29,305 --> 00:00:30,559
across several servers,

15
00:00:30,559 --> 00:00:34,394
it gets hard to remember what's running where.

16
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:37,930
Meet Outpost, the AI session manager

17
00:00:37,930 --> 00:00:39,346
that brings it all together.

18
00:00:39,346 --> 00:00:40,844
Your agents run on your servers,

19
00:00:40,844 --> 00:00:42,470
and they stay there.

20
00:00:42,470 --> 00:00:44,269
From your laptop, or your desktop,

21
00:00:44,269 --> 00:00:45,511
you see every session,

22
00:00:45,511 --> 00:00:48,510
on every server, in one place.

23
00:00:49,983 --> 00:00:52,189
Starting a session takes just a moment.

24
00:00:52,189 --> 00:00:54,604
Pick a server, give the session a name,

25
00:00:54,604 --> 00:00:56,415
and choose your agent.

26
00:00:56,415 --> 00:00:58,203
Then point it at a project folder,

27
00:00:58,203 --> 00:01:00,571
with suggestions as you type.

28
00:01:00,571 --> 00:01:03,067
If the agent isn't installed on that server yet,

29
00:01:03,067 --> 00:01:05,636
Outpost can install it for you.

30
00:01:07,117 --> 00:01:07,941
Click Connect,

31
00:01:07,941 --> 00:01:10,054
and open the session in your browser,

32
00:01:10,054 --> 00:01:13,897
or in Outpost Desktop, already attached and live.

33
00:01:13,897 --> 00:01:16,985
In the desktop app, each session gets its own tab,

34
00:01:16,985 --> 00:01:19,621
with your local shells right alongside.

35
00:01:19,621 --> 00:01:21,955
You see exactly what the agent is doing,

36
00:01:21,955 --> 00:01:25,372
and you can pick up the conversation right away.

37
00:01:26,650 --> 00:01:28,519
Because the session lives on the server,

38
00:01:28,519 --> 00:01:30,737
your connection is just a window into it.

39
00:01:30,737 --> 00:01:33,604
Close your laptop, or lose your Wi-Fi,

40
00:01:33,604 --> 00:01:35,709
and the agent keeps working.

41
00:01:35,961 --> 00:01:38,667
Later, reconnect from the same computer,

42
00:01:38,667 --> 00:01:39,770
or a different one,

43
00:01:39,770 --> 00:01:42,908
and you're right back where you left off.

44
00:01:44,383 --> 00:01:47,169
Need to show the agent a screenshot or a design?

45
00:01:47,169 --> 00:01:49,770
Just paste it, the way you always do.

46
00:01:49,770 --> 00:01:51,790
Image paste works seamlessly,

47
00:01:51,790 --> 00:01:54,704
in your browser and in the desktop app.

48
00:01:54,704 --> 00:01:58,086
No more fighting a remote clipboard.

49
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:01,695
Looking for an earlier conversation?

50
00:02:01,695 --> 00:02:04,017
Search a server by topic, phrase,

51
00:02:04,017 --> 00:02:07,593
or error message, and reopen the session you need.

52
00:02:07,593 --> 00:02:10,043
The search runs on the server itself.

53
00:02:10,043 --> 00:02:11,540
Your history stays there,

54
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:14,585
and only the matching snippets come back.

55
00:02:15,850 --> 00:02:17,638
With several agents running at once,

56
00:02:17,638 --> 00:02:19,345
Outpost shows you where you are needed,

57
00:02:19,345 --> 00:02:20,575
on every tab.

58
00:02:20,575 --> 00:02:22,456
You can see which agents are working,

59
00:02:22,456 --> 00:02:23,385
which are idle,

60
00:02:23,385 --> 00:02:24,349
and which have finished a

61
00:02:24,349 --> 00:02:26,439
turn and are waiting for you.

62
00:02:26,439 --> 00:02:27,936
Check in, and the notice clears,

63
00:02:27,936 --> 00:02:30,297
so you can move on to the next one.

64
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:33,408
And your servers stay simple.

65
00:02:33,408 --> 00:02:34,673
One self-contained terminal

66
00:02:34,673 --> 00:02:37,250
program keeps each session alive.

67
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:39,236
There's no manager service to run,

68
00:02:39,236 --> 00:02:41,360
and no extra ports to open.

69
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:43,520
The design also leaves room to grow,

70
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:45,203
including support for custom AI

71
00:02:45,203 --> 00:02:48,179
harnesses as your workflow evolves.

72
00:02:49,450 --> 00:02:51,099
Whichever computer you sit down at,

73
00:02:51,099 --> 00:02:52,422
your agents and conversations

74
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:54,442
are right where you left them.

75
00:02:54,442 --> 00:02:57,867
Outpost, the AI session manager.

76
00:02:57,867 --> 00:02:59,179
Keep the session.

77
00:02:59,179 --> 00:03:00,924
Keep your flow.
